<title>SINGAPORE: Sing Investments 96 net profit up 20 pct.</title>
<headline>Sing Investments 96 net profit up 20 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit				5.29   vs    4.41</p>
<p>    Dividend (cents)			6.00   vs    6.00</p>
<p>    Group shr (cents)		    11.64   vs    9.72</p>
<p>    Group shr (fully diluted)	  10.09   vs    8.56</p>
<p>    Operating Revenue		    32.80   vs   31.20</p>
<p>    Other income			    0.40   vs    0.61</p>
<p>    Investment income (loss)	    0.32   vs    0.01 (loss)</p>
<p>    Interest (expense)		   16.14   vs   15.74</p>
<p>    Depreciation/amortisation	   0.60   vs    0.52</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			  7.95   vs    7.16</p>
<p>    Tax					 2.66   vs    2.74</p>
<p>    Dividend pay date:		    June 20, 1997</p>
<p>    Last day books open:		  June 10, 1997</p>
<p>Note - Full name is Sing Investments &amp; Finance Ltd -- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
